/*
  The launcher label in Japanese. Its English counterpart is not here: it comes from
  INFOPLIST_KEY_CFBundleDisplayName in the xcconfigs, which is per configuration, so English
  distinguishes the flavors as "GitHub Search" and "GitHub Search Dev".

  This bundle is why the label is localised at all, and it is the same reason Android needs
  values-ja/: every *in-app* string comes from :core:designsystem's Compose resources, which the
  platform cannot read when it draws a home-screen label.

  There is deliberately no en.lproj. A .strings file wins over the Info.plist value for the
  language it covers, so adding one would replace the per-flavor English names with a single
  string and lose the distinction in both languages rather than one.

  Known asymmetry with Android, which has all four combinations of flavor and locale: on a
  Japanese device both flavors read「GitHub リポジトリ検索」, because a .strings file is a static
  resource and cannot vary per configuration the way src/dev/res/values-ja/ does. The prod name is
  the one chosen, since prod is what testers and reviewers install; the two builds are still
  separated by bundle identifier. Closing the gap properly needs a per-configuration copy phase
  selecting one of two ja.lproj directories, which is more machinery than a dev-only label in one
  locale is worth.
*/
"CFBundleDisplayName" = "GitHub リポジトリ検索";
